[center][size=6][b][color=#ef6a5a]A G E N T   A R M O R Y[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][i]Throw it. It does the aiming.[/i][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Agent-Armory/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/SeekerHero.jpg[/img][/center]

Every explosive in this game asks you to be in the right place at the right time. Aim the throw, judge the fuse, hope they are still standing there in three seconds.

[b]Agent Armory[/b] adds gadgets that do that part themselves. The first one is the [b]Cluster Seeker[/b]: a pod you throw, that follows you, and that bursts into [b]ten autonomous drones[/b] the moment something hostile gets close. They pick their own targets and detonate on contact.

[center][color=#ef6a5a]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]This is a beta - here is exactly what that means[/color][/b][/size]
The Seeker is finished and plays the way it is meant to. It is called a beta because of what is around it, and I would rather list that than let you find it:
[list]
[*][b]One game build, properly.[/b] V 3.1.0 was played through with this exact version - hand model, icon, sound, the pod landing and following, ten drones hunting, the skill entry, all looked at. [b]V 3.0.0 and V 3.0.1[/b] load cleanly and were played during development, but not on this build, so I am not going to write them down as if they were.
[*][b]The balance is a first draft.[/b] Ten drones, 180 damage each, unlocked at Explosives 35. Those numbers came from comparing against vanilla's throwables, not from a hundred hours of play. If it feels too strong, too weak, or unlocked at the wrong point, [b]say so in the Posts tab[/b] - that is the main thing I want out of a beta.
[*][b]One module of a planned set.[/b] The chem launcher, throwable turret, gun drone and hive are not in this file yet.
[/list]

[center][color=#ef6a5a]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]The Cluster Seeker[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Throw it, and that is the whole input.[/b] No pin to pull, no timer to set, no right-click to arm. The charge goes off on impact and the pod is out.
[*][b]The pod waits with you.[/b] With nothing in range it follows you around instead of sitting where it landed - so a pod you threw too early is not a pod you wasted.
[*][b]Ten seekers[/b] burst out when enemies come close. Each one picks its own target, chases it for up to 18 seconds, and detonates on contact for 180 damage in a 4 m radius.
[*][b]They split up.[/b] The drones divide the available targets between them rather than all ten piling onto the nearest zombie.
[*][b]It will not eat your base.[/b] The pod itself does 1 damage and no block damage worth the name. Everything that happens comes from the drones.
[/list]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Agent-Armory/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/SeekerSwarm.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][i]One throw, ten drones, and none of them waiting for you to aim.[/i][/center]

[center][size=4][b][color=#ef6a5a]▶ See it work[/color][/b][/size]
[url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pQ4O9ZTpW90]youtube.com/watch?v=pQ4O9ZTpW90[/url][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]What it is good at, and what it is not[/color][/b][/size]
This is not a bigger grenade. A contact grenade puts 341 damage into a five-metre circle the instant it lands, and against a tight crowd it will out-damage a Seeker.

What the Seeker buys you is [b]not having to be there[/b]. It works around a corner, it finds the straggler you did not see, and it keeps working while you back off and reload. Throw it into the room you are about to leave, not the one you are about to clear.

[b]It does almost nothing to blocks.[/b] Do not bring it to a safe or a horde base you are trying to demolish - that is what the Timed Charge and the rockets are for.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Agent-Armory/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/SeekerPod.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][i]Landed and waiting, with the horde still a street away. It keeps up with you until something comes close enough to be worth splitting for.[/i][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]How you get one[/color][/b][/size]
Two ways in, and either is enough:
[list]
[*][b]The Explosives skill unlocks it at level 35[/b] - the same rank as the Timed Charge, the last throwable before rockets. Read explosives magazines and you grow into it whether you were looking for it or not.
[*][b]The Cluster Seeker Schematic[/b] drops from loot and turns up at traders. Find one early and you get there ahead of the skill.
[/list]

Crafted at the [b]workbench[/b]: 3 mechanical parts, 18 gunpowder, 3 forged steel, 2 electrical parts, 2 springs. Stacks to 20.

[quote]Level 35 was chosen to sit beside the Timed Charge because the Seeker is a mid-game tool, not an endgame one - and because the whole point of hanging it on the skill was that people actually get to use it. Adding the mod to a save you are already deep into works: the skill route does not need you to find anything.[/quote]

[center][color=#ef6a5a]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Played and verified on V 3.1.0.[/b] [b]V 3.0.0 and V 3.0.1[/b] were launched and their logs checked - mod loads, Harmony patches apply, no errors, exceptions or XML problems - but they were not played through on this build, so they do not get the same word. Other 3.x builds are untested, not known-broken. The whole thing is a Harmony DLL, so every release has to re-earn this list from scratch.
[*][b]EasyAntiCheat must be off.[/b] This mod ships a Harmony DLL. Single-player and private servers.
[*][b]No other mods required.[/b]
[*][b]Multiplayer: everyone needs it, server included.[/b] 7 Days to Die does not send asset bundles from the server to the client, so a player without the mod installed cannot render the pod or the drones.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install the zip with Vortex or MO2, or extract the [i]AgentArmory[/i] folder into [i]7 Days To Die/Mods/[/i].
[*]Launch with EAC disabled.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]Adding and removing mid-save[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Adding it mid-save is fine[/b] - that is what the skill unlock is for.

[b]Removing it needs one moment of care:[/b] make sure no pod and no drone is alive in the world first. They are custom entity classes, and a save that still contains one cannot resolve it once the mod is gone. Let them run out, then remove the mod. Nothing else is touched - no blocks, no vanilla items, no world edits.

[size=5][b][color=#ef6a5a]Honest notes[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]The drones are ground units.[/b] They run at things, they do not fly. Stairs and rough terrain slow them down, and a target on a roof is a target they will not reach.
[*][b]18 seconds, then they are gone.[/b] Deliberately: ten guided explosives loose in the world with no time limit is a performance problem and a balance one.
[*][b]Kills count as yours.[/b] The drones carry the thrower's ID, so the XP and the kill credit come back to you.
[*][b]Localized into 13 languages[/b] - EN, DE, ES, FR, IT, JA, KO, PL, PT-BR, RU, TR, ZH-Hans, ZH-Hant.
[/list]

